WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.180
Speaker 1: We're continuing our look at whether&nbsp;
or not Fox News is abandoning Donald Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:11.280
in 2024. The answer seems to continue&nbsp;
to be they're not abandoning him yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:18.840
but they've got an ejection and ejection seat&nbsp;
and they could pull the lever at any time if it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.500
looks like things are going to go the direction&nbsp;
of Ron DeSantis. Here is yet another example.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:30.720
Stuart Varney interviewed Mitch McConnell's wife,&nbsp;
Elaine Chao. Elaine Chao was attacked by Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:37.620
Trump for her ethnicity. Now, multiple times&nbsp;
he's referred to her as Coco Chao. And what is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:43.980
interesting about this interview is that Stuart&nbsp;
Varney says, I mean, months too late, but Stuart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:51.720
Varney says we were all appalled here at Fox&nbsp;
News when Trump spoke about you that way, not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:55.860
sounding very Fox News like. Let's take a listen.
Speaker 3: I want to talk about inflation in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.860 --> 00:01:02.700
moment. But first, former President Trump attacked&nbsp;
you on the grounds of your ethnicity. I wonder if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:07.980
you'd like to take this moment to respond.
Speaker 2: Well, the president says many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:12.829
things. I don't make a point of&nbsp;
responding to his comments. Okay.&nbsp;

00:01:12.829 --> 00:01:17.220
Speaker 3: I'll leave it right there. We were&nbsp;
all appalled at what he said, and it's up to you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:22.380
what you said in response. Thank you very much.
Speaker 1: We were all appalled by what he said.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:28.800
So this is kind of interesting. There are&nbsp;
people making too much of this. You know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:36.120
the first thing is if everyone at Fox News was&nbsp;
appalled when Trump said. This about Elaine Chao&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:42.420
in what was the exact date, the very beginning&nbsp;
of October. It's almost the end of December&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:49.500
now. So they hid the they kept to themselves how&nbsp;
appalled they were about what Trump said until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:57.360
mid-December. So if they were indeed appalled,&nbsp;
they were not super eager to make it known. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:03.000
this is yet another one of those you don't really&nbsp;
have to read further into it. Then at face value,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:10.500
which is Fox News is maintaining a certain&nbsp;
distance from Trump under notice that even since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:16.560
announcing that he was running in 2024, I don't&nbsp;
believe Trump had like a serious interview on Fox&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:21.180
News. I don't even know if he's appeared at all.&nbsp;
Fox News is keeping a respectful distance to Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:28.380
while continuing to have pro-Trump and&nbsp;
anti-Trump voices from the right on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:32.760
channel. Fox News doesn't know the direction&nbsp;
it's going to go. We know that the Murdochs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:36.600
would prefer someone other than Trump be the&nbsp;
Republican nominee and ultimately president,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:41.160
and they're just leaving themselves that&nbsp;
possibility open. It's not the biggest deal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:47.160
but they just want to be prepared with an escape&nbsp;
hatch if indeed the tide truly turns against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:53.160
Trump. That's what's going on here. Let's not make&nbsp;
more of it than it is. But it is something that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:58.740
that's the way FOX News is approaching the 2024&nbsp;
primaries so far. We'll have all of these clips&nbsp;&nbsp;

